    "verdict": "PARTIAL REPLICATION",
    "summary": "RECH-X significantly beats RealGARCH on US_SPY (paper's headline claim reproduced on those markets). The RNN adds NO significant value over the linear GARCH-X at H=1 or H=5 in any market; only a marginal H=22 edge in US_SPY, US_QQQ, TW_TX. Against the pre-specified GJR(1,1) ceiling, RECH-X is significantly WORSE on TW_TX. Net: any RECH-X advantage traces to the RV covariate (captured equally by linear GARCH-X) and/or a single long horizon, not to the deep-learning recurrence \u2014 consistent with the project's ML-ceiling finding.",
